    "description": "Central National Bank Manhattan refurbish pole sign including message center option 4\nAt Central National Bank's 1403 College Ave branch in Manhattan, option 4:\n1) check in/out with branch manager Doug Haverkamp\n2) survey signs, including the main pylon sign\n3) coordinate schedules with the bank, the assistance of a shielded bucket truck and Luminous Neon’s Hutchinson shop\n4) remove the logo cabinets to refurbish the logo cabinet and replace the time & temperature with it being gone approximately three weeks\n5) provide and install two 3’ x 8’ digitally printed banners with Central National Bank’s logo to be there while the cabinets are gone, take temporary completion photos\n6) remove neon and fluorescent components\n7) repaint the logo cabinet PMS 288 blue, paint reveals to match limestone\n8) remove peeling white vinyl on push-thru letters and overlay new white translucent vinyl\n9) provide and install new blue Flexi-Brite LED strips and power supplies for former neon accents\n10) remove & scrap existing time & temperature unit\n11) provide and install a new 2’5” x 7’3” 8mm full-color Watchfire message center to replace the existing time & temperature, including broadband wireless communications with filler panels painted to match the limestone\n12) for the inset ATM cabinets, replace both faces to read ATM • ITM with reverse 3630-157 Sultan blue vinyl, paint retainers/cabinets PMS 288 blue\n13) provide and install new white LED Kwik Stiks/LED pods and power supplies in the logo cabinet and ATM cabinets\n14) reinstall cabinets and remove banners\n15) take completion photos\nDrawing VB-J34933\nNOTES:  If needed, primary power by others.  Logo cabinet & ATM • ITM cabinets require a separate circuit(s); message center requires 120 volt, 30 amp, single phase service, 15 amps per face, with circuits to be hot 24 hours a day.",
